SM(162,{"n":"Luke 18.15-34","a":"Fr Stephen De Young Archives/Luke 18.15-34.mp3","d":3417.5,"s":[[0.3,"We're going to pick up here in Luke chapter 18, verse 15."],[6.3,"And by way of my usual non-introduction, introduction, if you want to hear from way back when, many moons ago, when we had the introduction to the Gospel of Luke, that's back in the first, very first Bible study."],[23.98,"It's available on the website."],[27.9,"To sort of get us caught up to where we are right now."],[44.06,"We talked about how sort of in broad strokes what we have in uh St."],[50.62,"Luke's Gospel is after after the beginning, where we read about the birth of St."],[55.34,"John the Forerunner, Saint John the Baptist, and the birth of Christ, after that sort of prologue."],[61.54,"We've seen Christ's ministry begin in Galilee, and then his journey through Samaria down to Judea."],[70.26,"And now we've seen his sort of teaching in Judea while he's on his way to Jerusalem."],[75.62,"Uh we are getting much closer to Jerusalem now."],[78.42,"In fact, probably before we finish this evening, we'll be at least on the outskirts of the city."],[88.18,"Um as I said, uh, since Jesus has come to Judea, we've been reading sort of a series of sections from Saint Luke, um, describing sort of aspects of his teaching, recountings of his teaching."],[103.7,"We had the dinner party at the Pharisees' house."],[106.1,"We had some other interactions with the Pharisees, we've had some interactions with his disciples and with the people who were following him along the way."],[115.3,"And we're sort of in the midst of in the midst of one of those right now."],[121.06,"Um before we start, I do want to make a note because of some questions, some questions I was asked."],[127.86,"I know I've mentioned this before, but it's been a while, I think."],[132.18,"So I'm going to talk about it, I'm going to talk about it again."],[136.98,"Uh one of the problems, I'll go ahead and call it a problem."],[145.3,"In uh in Bible study and in talking about the Bible, if you get books about the Bible, if you make the mistake I frequently do of watching TV documentaries about the Bible, um, or watching YouTube videos, even worse, because there's no quality control about the Bible."],[166.14,"One of the sort of presuppositions, one of the sort of presuppositions that people have, is that the sort of the earliest and the oldest form of the text is the best form of the text, or the real form of the text."],[188.46,"Sometimes it even goes beyond that."],[190.22,"Sometimes it goes to, well, we need to go try and get past the text of the Bible and get to what really happened."],[197.9,"Right? That's sort of behind."],[201.1,"Behind the text."],[204.62,"And there are a number of problems with this."],[209.26,"Because, for example, and when I've talked about this before, I've talked about it in terms of other things."],[215.26,"For example, towards the tendency people have to want to sort of try and harmonize the gospels, try and take the four gospels and smush them together, you know, to make one story."],[225.42,"That's essentially a form of this of what I'm talking about."],[228.94,"Well, we need to get at what really happened behind these four gospels."],[233.1,"So, you know, uh St."],[234.94,"John says that Jesus cleansed the temple at the beginning of his ministry."],[239.26,"Well, I shouldn't say that."],[240.38,"He doesn't say he did the beginning of his ministry."],[242.22,"As you're reading the Gospel of John, one of the first stories you read is Jesus cleansing the temple."],[247.66,"The other three Gospels, that comes right at the end."],[253.18,"And so you will see people, and this has a long pedigree, St."],[256.86,"John Chrysostom did this, uh, saying, you know, well, Jesus must have cleansed the temple twice."],[264.62,"Right? He did it once at the beginning and then once at the end."],[268.22,"Well, none of the four Gospels said he did it twice."],[268.46,"Right? Right? Not a one of them."],[277.86,"They all say he did it once."],[279.86,"Right? And so what you've done now is you've made your own version of the story that doesn't correspond to any of the four."],[288.02,"Or one of the really common ones, and I know I've mentioned this before, but this is going to destroy a lot of really nice sermons and Easter pageants."],[296.9,"But the seven last words of Jesus from the cross."],[301.14,"None of the four Gospels said that Jesus said seven things from the cross."],[309.3,"The four gospels have him saying different things."],[312.98,"If you tally those up, you end up with seven."],[316.5,"But none of the gospels say he said all seven."],[320.74,"So when you put them all together, you've made your own version of the story that's different than all four gospels."],[329.38,"Those are sort of the nicer ways of doing it."],[331.38,"You know, History Channel, a National Geographic Channel, you get more like, well, none of this really happened."],[337.3,"Here's what the historical Jesus really said and did and what he was really like."],[342.9,"Right? You get that kind of thing."],[344.58,"But that's basically the same thing."],[346.1,"That's coming up with another version of the story."],[349.78,"Right? Other than the four that we have."],[356.1,"And you will see this done in other ways."],[358.66,"You will see people go and try and chop up the text itself."],[361.94,"They'll say, well, this half of the verse, you know, isn't in the oldest manuscripts."],[367.86,"An example we saw already in Mark and Luke."],[373.62,"Remember the episode where Jesus returns to his disciples, they've been trying to cast the demon out of the boy."],[380.62,"Right. And after Jesus sort of upbraids them for their lack of faith, what does he say?"],[387.34,"This kind only comes out through prayer."],[391.42,"Right. The earliest manuscripts don't have the and fasting part."],[398.54,"Now, as much as I'd like to leave that out personally, as you can tell from looking at me."],[409.02,"The assumption there is."],[411.74,"The assumption there is, well, if that wasn't in the original, quote unquote the original, then we don't have to worry about it."],[422.78,"We can ignore it."],[423.74,"That's not, quote unquote, really in the Bible."],[428.22,"And so you will get all kinds of arguments toward that kind of thing."],[432.46,"The story we're going to read in a little while about Christ's sweating blood in the Gospel of Luke isn't in the oldest manuscripts."],[454.86,"Why this is a problem is, first of all, we don't have any access to quote unquote what really happened, other than the four gospels."],[466.94,"So anything else you're going to say happened that doesn't correspond to one of the four Gospels is conjecture."],[473.42,"You're making it up, essentially."],[475.98,"You're guessing. Because we have no access to it."],[482.02,"Second problem, this is one of those tautologies, the Bible is the Bible."],[489.54,"And what I mean by that is the more you study the Bible, the more messy things kind of get."],[504.26,"So, for example, when people are trying to say, well, it's the original."],[508.42,"Right? It's the original that has authority."],[511.62,"Okay. Well, let's let's look at, I know we're not there yet, but let's look at 2 Corinthians."],[518.58,"Okay. We say, we all agree, St."],[521.7,"Paul wrote 2 Corinthians."],[524.02,"What does that mean?"],[526.26,"Because he tells us in 2 Corinthians, he's not sitting there with a pen writing it."],[531.54,"Right. He's speaking, and a scribe is writing it down."],[538.5,"Even assuming he's speaking Greek."],[543.86,"He's speaking Greek, it's being written in Greek."],[547.22,"Do you think his secretary wasn't doing part of his job, which was to correct the grammar?"],[555.94,"Right? So what's the original?"],[558.02,"Is it what came out of St."],[559.78,"Paul's mouth? Or is what the scribe wrote down?"],[565.46,"Common practice after that, and we have examples of St."],[568.26,"Paul doing this in the text, is that after that, the person who dictated the letter would read it over and make corrections if there was something they didn't like and then sort of sign it at the end."],[580.5,"Remember one of his letters, St."],[581.78,"Paul says, you know, see, I'm writing this with my own hand."],[585.5,"That he's sort of signing it at the end."],[587.98,"Right. So then which is the original?"],[590.46,"Is it what the secretary wrote down St."],[593.66,"Paul dictated? Or is it the version after his corrections?"],[599.42,"Second Corinthians gets even more complicated."],[602.46,"Because 2 Corinthians is made up of at least two letters."],[605.26,"We'll talk about that more when we get there."],[609.34,"It's St. Paul actually wrote four letters to the Corinthians."],[613.82,"2 Corinthians is made up of parts of two of them put together."],[620.94,"So when you say the original 2 Corinthians, do you mean the two letters?"],[627.9,"Do you mean the two letters in their entirety, or just the parts that ended up being in 2 Corinthians?"],[635.82,"Not only that, around 100 AD, Christians took all of Paul's letters and Hebrews."],[646.78,"This is why why in the church we refer to it as St."],[649.9,"Paul's Epistle to the Hebrews, because it was part of that collection."],[653.98,"Even though the church fathers read it and read St."],[656.7,"Paul's letters and said, This doesn't look like it's written by the same guy, but it was part of that collection."],[662.14,"Collected it all together and edited it at that time."],[675.5,"The original? Or is it the way it was separately?"],[683.42,"Because every manuscript we have, every copy of 2 Corinthians that still exists is from that collection."],[695.22,"That's the only one we have access to."],[697.94,"So this idea that it's the original, that somehow we have to pursue quote unquote the original, it doesn't work."],[706.26,"It doesn't work."],[708.66,"So now I'm going to say another tautology."],[712.34,"The version of the scriptures that has authority in the church is the version of the scriptures that has authority in the church."],[723.54,"Meaning there is a version of these texts."],[727.7,"There are a lot of them out there."],[728.82,"You go and look at all the there's close to 6,000 manuscripts of the New Testament."],[735.14,"Okay? 6,000 handwritten copies."],[740.26,"Ranging from the 2nd century up to the 15th century."],[745.14,"There are actually some more after that, but we're not counting those because those are so late."],[754.74,"None of them are identical."],[758.42,"Why? Well, because they're hand copied."],[760.42,"So people make spelling mistakes."],[762.82,"I mean, it's not confused."],[763.7,"It's not like we don't know what it says, because you could tell when there's a spelling mistake, because you have 5,999 other copies."],[770.98,"So you could go, okay, this guy just made a spelling mistake."],[773.94,"Or this guy just left a word out."],[775.86,"Or this guy was, it was late at night and he skipped a line."],[778.66,"Right? They're even somewhere they skipped a page."],[781.3,"Right? But we could tell because we have all these other copies."],[784.34,"So it's not like we don't know what it says."],[786.02,"But there's all these copies."],[787.94,"And they're all different."],[791.3,"But there is one that has been used by the church."],[797.26,"It's like you've got all these branches of the stream."],[800.14,"But there's one stream that's been used in the church, that's been read in the church, that's been prayed by the church, that's been quoted by the church."],[810.14,"For the last 2,000 years."],[815.74,"And so the version that has authority is not some hypothetical original."],[823.18,"Right? It's not some hypothetical event that the original was written about."],[829.18,"Right. The version that has authority is the version that has had authority."],[836.46,"And so this is why, you know, I don't think anyone here has been overly shocked by it."],[841.66,"Maybe I said it too fast."],[843.02,"But when I've said things like, the thine is the kingdom and the power of the glory wasn't originally at the end of the Lord's Prayer in the Gospels, that was added by the church later."],[855.66,"This is why that's not a problem for us."],[860.14,"Because we as Orthodox Christians don't believe that God sort of inspired St."],[865.9,"Paul one day in 45 AD to write Galatians, and then Galatians just got thrown out there into the world."],[876.38,"Right? For who knows what to happen to it over the course of 2,000 years."],[879.98,"And now we gotta just do the best we can to try to figure out what it was that the Holy Spirit inspired St."],[885.74,"Paul to say."],[886.62,"The same Holy Spirit who inspired St."],[889.58,"Paul on that day in 45 AD to write Galatians is the same spirit who lives and dwells in the church and leads us to Christ."],[900.5,"It's the same spirit who was there, and the people who were copying the manuscripts, who were reading those manuscripts in church, who were preaching on those manuscripts, the fathers who were quoting those manuscripts, it's the same Holy Spirit all the way through, guiding the whole process."],[921.14,"So the scriptures we have now are the scriptures that God has given us now."],[928.98,"And all of this archaeology, well, kind of interesting, you know, it's kind of interesting to see how the text developed and how things changed and to look at different things."],[938.98,"You know, oh, this church father quotes this verse a little differently than this other church father."],[942.98,"Well, that's all interesting to nerds like me."],[945.78,"Right? It's not germane to what version of the scriptures has authority over how we live our life, how we understand who Christ is and come to know him."],[958.26,"That's the scriptures that we have today in the church."],[963.46,"I say I went through all that because, like I said, I had some questions from people, you know, and there are a lot of discussions about this."],[973.06,"Um, and we we need to sort of understand that and at least be able to give somebody else some idea about that."],[982.82,"Because this is our our Protestant friends spend an inordinate amount of time arguing about this because of their views of inerrancy and their views of right?"],[995.38,"They say, well, it's anerrant the originals."],[997.38,"Well, we don't have the originals, you know."],[999.62,"So, you know, as if all of the original."],[1002.74,"Well, you know, and so there's a lot of you know, the whole fundamentalist liberal debate, all this sort of stuff."],[1012.78,"And you get bogged down in it to the point that you don't hear what scripture is saying anymore."],[1019.58,"You're so busy arguing about whether the Exodus literally happened exactly the way it says in the book of Exodus and what year it was and what Pharaoh was Pharaoh, and all this kind of stuff, that you miss the point, right, of what the text is trying to teach us."],[1036.3,"First of all, about how God deals with his people, and then second, secondly, and probably even more importantly than that, or more specific than that, what it teaches us about Christ."],[1046.54,"Right? Because, as we're gonna read coming up here in Luke, when Christ dies and rises again, he does it at Passover, and that's not a coincidence."],[1056.78,"So you can kind of miss the forest for the trees when you when you get down into the weeds, into the weeds of that stuff."],[1066.14,"Okay, and so that's why that's why I went through that again."],[1071.26,"That's not something that we need to engage in, it's not an argument we need to have."],[1076.46,"We have the scriptures, God has given them to us through his Holy Spirit, and they're here to help lead us to Christ, and so we can study them as we have them without having to pull all this, pull all this apart."],[1093.74,"And a brief footnote to that, just real quick, um a big part of why is that, and again, this is this is an important part of the Orthodox Church in our understanding and our understanding of the Holy Spirit being still with us, is that through the power of the Holy Spirit, Christ is still with us."],[1116.02,"This is why in the liturgy we say that Christ is in our midst."],[1119.62,"Alright, Christ is still with us."],[1121.62,"In the West."],[1123.62,"Well, they don't often put it this way."],[1126.66,"Once Christ ascends into heaven, if you're a Protestant, he ascends into heaven and he left us a book."],[1135.14,"And that book, the Bible, is how we come to know Christ now."],[1141.3,"Right? That's how we come to know Christ."],[1143.06,"That's how we come to know how to worship, that's how we come to know everything."],[1145.62,"If you're a Roman Catholic, Christ ascended into heaven and he sent us a vicar."],[1150.98,"Right? He ascended into heaven and he put Saint Peter in charge."],[1155.7,"St. Peter passed it on to the next and the next and the next."],[1160.34,"So if you want to know what's true, you don't look at the Bible, you go and the Pope tells you what's true."],[1166.74,"Right? The teaching mag teaching magisterium of the church tells you what's true."],[1170.66,"Right? They tell you what the Bible is, they tell you what the Bible means, they tell you what tradition is, they tell you what tradition means."],[1177.54,"Neither of those is what the scriptures actually say."],[1180.42,"What the scriptures actually say, we just celebrated the ascension, is that Christ ascended into heaven and left us the Holy Spirit."],[1194.98,"Continues to reveal Christ to us, continues to reveal Christ to us through the scriptures, and through the church."],[1205.3,"And so when we talk about tradition, we're talking about the life of the Holy Spirit in the church."],[1210.66,"We're not talking about something that bishops whisper to each other in back rooms and hand it down."],[1215.42,"We're talking about the Spirit living in the church, who has lived in the church in every generation of the church since the beginning."],[1224.3,"And so this is why we can trust the scriptures we have now."],[1228.94,"Because it's not the result of a series of historical accidents."],[1233.9,"It's the result of the working of the Holy Spirit in the church."],[1240.46,"So all that said, unless anybody has any questions."],[1255.1,"Yeah. So how could I explain with them what they're saying with their mindset?"],[1262.54,"Right. Well, part of the part of the issue there isn't just with Protestantism, it's with Western theology."],[1271.58,"I don't want to go too far into the weeds here."],[1275.02,"But Western theology is sort of innately binatarian."],[1283.74,"And it's because of the Filioque clause."],[1287.58,"The Holy Spirit proceeds from the Father and the Son."],[1291.66,"Binatarian as opposed to Trinitarian."],[1293.82,"Two instead of three."],[1305.94,"The Arians argued that because the Logos is right, Christ, God the Son, is begotten of the Father."],[1320.98,"And the Holy Spirit proceeds from the Father."],[1325.06,"That only the Father is really God then."],[1328.5,"Because the other two sort of come forth from him."],[1334.34,"Which is a bad argument."],[1336.82,"Right? Because it's a circular argument."],[1340.34,"What makes the Father the Father is that he's unbegotten and doesn't proceed."],[1344.66,"Right? And so they're saying, well, only the Father can be God, therefore only the Father is God."],[1351.94,"That's why it's a circular argument."],[1355.46,"But rather than responding by pointing out it's a circular argument, the West created the Filioque clause that said, oh, well, the Holy Spirit proceeds from the Son too."],[1363.94,"So see, both the Father and the Son are the sources of divinity."],[1371.22,"What's the problem with that?"],[1374.1,"Who proceeds from the Holy Spirit?"],[1378.18,"So then, by their own definition, is the Holy Spirit God."],[1385.22,"See the problem?"],[1387.78,"And so what happens in that kind of thinking regarding the Trinity is that the Holy Spirit gets kind of demoted."],[1394.9,"He has sort of this subordinate status."],[1397.78,"Now they're not going to say he's subordinated."],[1400.26,"They'll deny that."],[1401.86,"But the construct sort of does that, right, automatically, because they've already posited in order to be God, you have to sort of be a source of Godhead for another person, and then they've said that the Holy Spirit isn't."],[1415.74,"And so that's why, in not just Protestant theology, but in a lot of Roman Catholic theology, the Holy Spirit is kind of depersonalized."],[1424.3,"He's sort of like the force in Star Wars."],[1429.66,"He's sort of a feeling or an energy, or right his personhood."],[1438.38,"Is this and his status in the Holy Trinity, that he proceeds from the Father and comes to rest in the Son and the unity of the Trinity and the Father."],[1449.26,"All that kind of vanishes."],[1452.46,"And so there's a basic misunderstanding of the Holy Spirit in all Western theology."],[1460.22,"And it manifests itself in different ways."],[1462.86,"You either get, you know, Pentecostalism, where all you talk about is the Holy Spirit."],[1468.62,"And or you get most Protestant churches where you barely talk about the Holy Spirit."],[1478.54,"Right. Right. Yeah, it's focused almost entirely on Christ."],[1486.54,"So the correct way to respond to that, you have to start back a step."],[1492.38,"And start talking about the Holy Trinity."],[1495.1,"Start talking about these are three persons who are all equally God."],[1501.74,"Right. And that there's only one God, and that that unity is found in the Father."],[1512.14,"And so that gets very deep."],[1514.22,"And I went into the weeds, like I said, I didn't want to."],[1517.98,"But that's that's really where you have to start."],[1520.3,"You have to start, and and a good place to take them in the scriptures, and I'll sort of end this part of the discussion with this."],[1527.42,"The good place to take them uh in the scriptures is take them to uh John chapter 16 on, 16 through 19, basically."],[1537.86,"Where Christ is talking about sending the Spirit and what the Spirit will do and how the Spirit's going to work in the in the church."],[1547.06,"Sort of take them through that."],[1548.02,"And the way that the way that Christ talks about the Spirit, the way he talks about the Spirit relating to him, the way he talks about the Spirit relating to the Father."],[1557.94,"I think that's probably the best place to take them and get them to start thinking about that and start thinking about the Trinity in a different way."],[1566.9,"Okay. Okay. So unless there's anything else, we'll go ahead and get started."],[1571.54,"Now that I've gone way into various matters theological."],[1578.74,"Okay. So Luke chapter 18, verse 15."],[1583.7,"Then they also brought infants to him that he might touch them."],[1587.22,"When the disciples saw it, they rebuked them."],[1592.34,"Now we've talked before about kids, but it bears repeating."],[1595.86,"Right? The view of children in the ancient world was very different than the view of children today."],[1602.42,"Right. Um, you know, we we just love little kids."],[1606.58,"Oh, this is babies cute."],[1608.58,"You know, little kids are cute, little kids are great, you know."],[1613.38,"Uh some of us want to sort of pad the whole world for kids."],[1617.06,"We have to scrutinize what we allow on TV with it, because a kid might see it, you know."],[1624.5,"To say the least, the ancient world was not that way."],[1628.02,"Not that way."],[1629.38,"Um, we've talked before about sort of Roman family structures."],[1633.7,"Um, it's worthwhile, and I don't want to go into the weeds on this."],[1640.38,"Uh, it's you know, we talk about the sort of the horrors of abortion in this country."],[1645.58,"But we have to remember not only did they have abortion in the Roman world, uh they exposed infants."],[1655.1,"When a baby was born, the baby was taken to the Potter Familius, who is the head of household."],[1660.78,"Literally means the father of the family."],[1662.54,"But we have to remember we're talking about extended families."],[1666.06,"This wasn't mom, dad, and the kids."],[1668.14,"This was mom, dad, the kids, the grandkids, maybe an uncle, aunt, cousin."],[1673.02,"The whole extended family."],[1674.54,"The head of that whole family, sort of the patriarch of the family, grandpa, great grandpa, right, whoever it was with the Potter Familius."],[1682.3,"Anyone in that household had a baby, it was brought to the Potter Familius, Potter Familius sort of inspected it, thought about things economically and etc."],[1691.9,"etc. Who the father was, what was going on, decided whether to accept it or not."],[1697.02,"If he decided not to accept it, they took the baby out and left it in the woods to die."],[1704.7,"Yes. Right? Letters for the first century."],[1717.66,"Husband writing home to his wife, who just had a baby."],[1721.42,"If it's a boy, keep it."],[1722.62,"If it's a girl, take care of it."],[1724.7,"Meaning, go abandon it."],[1728.86,"This was just common and accepted."],[1731.26,"One of the things early Christians used to do was go and find these babies and adopt them."],[1738.38,"Because, of course, the early Christians were completely opposed to this, to this practice."],[1744.18,"But it was a common, common Roman practice."],[1748.82,"So kids were not seen as this blessing from God."],[1753.38,"Kids were not seen"],[1754.59,"Because, you know, it was it was up to you whether you wanted to raise this kid or not."],[1760.03,"And if you didn't."],[1763.31,"Get rid of it."],[1764.27,"Kids were kind of a nuisance."],[1766.59,"Right. The Jews did not."],[1770.51,"The Jews did not."],[1772.03,"By and large."],[1773.47,"I mean, I'm sure there were Hellenized Jews in different parts of the empire who may have participated in it."],[1778.19,"But in Judea, that kind of thing would frown upon."],[1784.11,"So, again, with that being a commonly accepted practice, you can imagine what that does to your view of children."],[1792.67,"So, you know, kids who are running around in the streets were sort of one step up from stray dogs."],[1798.35,"They're usually running around begging and stuff, you know."],[1801.95,"So when the disciples, when they're bringing these these kids to see Jesus, right, and the disciples say, uh, get out of here."],[1809.47,"They're not just being grumpy old men."],[1812.99,"Get out of here, kid."],[1814.27,"You know, young punks, get off my lawn, you know."],[1817.79,"It's not like that."],[1819.15,"Okay, this is this they're reflecting the common societal attitude of just like, oh, get these kids out of it, you know what I mean?"],[1826.03,"Like the way they'd shoe off a stray dog that came around begging, you know, or a stray cat."],[1831.23,"You know, eh, get out of here."],[1837.71,"But Jesus called them to him."],[1842.75,"The them here is the disciples."],[1846.43,"Called the disciples to him."],[1848.59,"And said, Let the little children come to me, and do not forbid them, for such is the kingdom of God."],[1854.19,"Assuredly I say to you, whoever does not receive the kingdom of God is a little child, will by no means enter it."],[1862.03,"Now, sometimes, the reason I went through all that in terms of the ancient view of children, sometimes when you hear people read this passage and interpret it, what does it mean to be like a child?"],[1872.83,"And they do it based on our modern view of children."],[1875.59,"They say, oh, being like being innocent."],[1879.91,"And kind and trusting, you know, and loving."],[1884.95,"You've got to remember that's not the view of children at the time."],[1889.35,"What Jesus is saying here is this is an illustration of what he's been saying, what we've seen him say in the last few passages about the last being first and the first being last."],[1901.59,"Right. We've got a group of people, we just had the parable of the Pharisee and the publican."],[1911.11,"Right? Where the Pharisee thought he was pretty great."],[1914.79,"And the publican realized he wasn't much."],[1919.75,"Right? But asked for God's mercy."],[1924.95,"This is a reflection on the same kind of idea when he says of such as the kingdom of heaven."],[1930.79,"These sort of cast off kids."],[1938.63,"You know, dependents."],[1941.99,"Right. This is the this is, you need to set yourself in the lowest place."],[1949.03,"Right? The lowest place if you want to enter the kingdom."],[1954.31,"So this is about humility."],[1956.63,"When he says they need to be like children."],[1959.83,"It's not about being sweet or innocent or cute or any of those other things we associate with it."],[1970.55,"So we're now about to have."],[1973.59,"We have the Pharisee and the publican."],[1975.43,"If the kids are like the publican."],[1978.35,"Now we're going to get another example of the same thing, but in the other direction."],[1984.43,"Now a certain ruler asked him, saying, Good teacher, what shall I do to inherit eternal life?"],[1994.43,"Now when it says ruler, you may wonder, what is this guy?"],[1997.95,"Isn't king from somewhere?"],[2001.79,"The word in Greek is actually archon."],[2005.95,"Right, which is Archon now."],[2008.75,"Basically, leader would probably be a better translation than ruler."],[2014.43,"This is a leading citizen."],[2016.11,"Right? A prominent, a prominent citizen."],[2020.35,"A prominent citizen of Judea, not Roman citizen."],[2023.31,"So this is this is someone who's important in the community in Judea."],[2027.95,"This is not just, these are not the peasants from Galilee who Jesus is speaking from before."],[2033.87,"This is one of the quote-unquote important people."],[2039.47,"And he comes to Jesus and says, Good teacher, what shall I do to inherit eternal life?"],[2048.19,"So Jesus said to him, Why do you call me good?"],[2051.55,"No one is good but one that is God."],[2056.75,"Now, is Jesus saying that he is not good?"],[2064.03,"So what is he saying?"],[2069.55,"That he's God."],[2072.35,"That he's God."],[2074.99,"Right. Because he approaches him and says, Good teacher."],[2079.91,"Right? Good teacher, while it's kissing up a little bit."],[2085.59,"And while it's respectful."],[2088.79,"Is that what Jesus is?"],[2090.79,"He's just a good rabbi."],[2092.55,"There's a bunch of rabbis."],[2094.79,"I've gotten opinions from these other rabbis."],[2097.11,"Let me get opinions from this rabbi."],[2100.15,"Right? Nora on collecting spiritual advice."],[2104.63,"You know, of how I should be, how I should be a good person."],[2108.39,"Right? What does this rabbi say?"],[2110.39,"About what's important."],[2112.23,"Is that who Jesus is in relation to this man?"],[2116.47,"No. Right? No."],[2118.31,"So what Jesus is doing here is he's questioning the man's approach."],[2122.55,"Right? Because when Jesus speaks, and when Jesus answers this question."],[2129.75,"He's going to answer it in a way that's authoritative."],[2134.15,"Jesus doesn't say things to people and say, well, here, think about this."],[2138.15,"Decide if it's useful."],[2140.79,"Right? You know?"],[2142.55,"Maybe, maybe not."],[2143.59,"You know, maybe, you know."],[2145.11,"It doesn't work for you."],[2147.51,"Right? Jesus doesn't give advice."],[2149.75,"Right? He gives authoritative instruction."],[2153.91,"Okay? And so, if Jesus is going to answer this question, he's answering it in that context."],[2159.19,"That's what he said."],[2165.03,"He says, You know the commandments."],[2166.63,"Do not commit adultery, do not murder, do not steal, do not bear false witness, honor your father and mother your mother."],[2172.63,"So he quotes some of the Ten Commandments."],[2175.03,"Right. Because you you know."],[2177.91,"Right? Why does he point out that you know?"],[2183.43,"He's still questioning his approach."],[2186.23,"Right? What must I do to inherit eternal life?"],[2189.03,"Right? Well, you're a prominent person around here."],[2192.67,"Right? You've been to a synagogue."],[2195.95,"You've heard the law."],[2196.91,"What does it say in Deuteronomy?"],[2198.27,"He who does Deuteronomy, he who does these things will live by them."],[2201.95,"Right? Eternal life."],[2205.63,"Keep the commandment."],[2206.99,"Why are you asking me this question?"],[2212.03,"Right? You should already know."],[2215.79,"And he said, All these things I have kept from my youth."],[2220.19,"Who does that sound like earlier this chapter?"],[2224.99,"Remember our friend the Pharisee, the Pharisee of the publican?"],[2228.35,"Right? Thank you that I'm not like these other men."],[2230.75,"I fast two days a week."],[2233.47,"I tithe, I do this, I do that."],[2236.03,"I do all these things."],[2240.11,"Right? Therefore, I'm one of the righteous people."],[2242.75,"Remember? I'm one of the righteous people."],[2246.99,"This guy comes up, what?"],[2249.15,"Good teacher. What's your opinion?"],[2252.11,"As an equal."],[2255.07,"What's your opinion?"],[2256.11,"What do you need to do to inherit eternal life?"],[2258.03,"Jesus says, Well, you know, you know the commandments."],[2262.03,"Right. And he says, Oh, I've I've done all those things since I was a child."],[2267.15,"Right. Now we know he was a teenager at some point, so we know that's a lie."],[2271.47,"Right? But so when Jesus heard these things."],[2280.43,"So don't notice the phrasing here."],[2283.15,"When Jesus hears his response."],[2285.63,"Now he knows who this person is."],[2287.95,"Right. He said to him, You still lack one thing."],[2293.71,"He says, okay."],[2296.47,"For the sake of argument."],[2299.67,"You've kept all the commandments from your youth."],[2301.99,"Okay. Just do one more thing."],[2304.47,"You'll inherit eternal life."],[2308.07,"Sell all that you have and distribute to the poor, and you will have treasure in heaven and come follow me."],[2316.07,"Right? You're a prominent citizen, you're wealthy."],[2320.63,"Take all that stuff you've got, sell it, give it to the poor, come become one of my disciples."],[2325.75,"You'll inherit eternal life."],[2327.27,"Now, is he being sarcastic?"],[2329.27,"No, no. No, if he does this, he will inherit eternal life."],[2333.59,"This is an honest answer."],[2336.07,"Right. This is an honest answer."],[2338.31,"This is what this man needs to do if he wants to inherit eternal life."],[2345.27,"But when he heard this, he became very sorrowful, for he was very rich."],[2353.83,"Because he was very rich."],[2355.59,"He had a lot of stuff."],[2358.95,"Gotta keep your stuff."],[2375.75,"For it is easier for a camel to go through the eye of a needle than for a rich man to enter the kingdom of God."],[2384.15,"So Jesus sees his response, which obviously was visible."],[2389.11,"Right? He made the sad face emoji."],[2391.75,"Right. After hearing this."],[2395.63,"Right? He was visibly distraught because he wasn't going to do what Jesus had said."],[2404.75,"And so Jesus says, How hard is it?"],[2407.47,"Now, you know, we typically think of this as an actual like needle and thread needle and trying to shove a camel through it."],[2415.79,"There's some debate as to whether the eye of the needle is actually a reference to a particular gate, small gate to the city, and trying to shove a camel through it."],[2423.39,"Either way, you get the idea."],[2426.19,"It's very difficult."],[2427.87,"Now it's interesting."],[2429.31,"You could go and see this in Italy to this day, but the Medici family, who was insanely wealthy in the 16th and 17th century."],[2438.03,"Their family chapel at their estates."],[2451.15,"Because they wanted to communicate the fact that they were going to make it."],[2456.11,"Even though they were insanely wealthy."],[2460.59,"Right. Now, this we've seen already, this has been a recurring theme in St."],[2467.87,"Luke's gospel. Where, you know, for example, in uh Matthew 5, in the Beatitudes, we saw blessed are the poor in spirit."],[2478.43,"Right? Remember in St."],[2479.55,"Luke's version, it was just blessed are the poor."],[2483.15,"Period. Right. Uh, where St."],[2487.23,"Luke tends to speak more literally in terms of wealth and poverty."],[2492.99,"As we've said before, this is not saying wealthy people are bad, poor people are all good."],[2502.43,"Right? That's not what St."],[2504.27,"Luke is getting at."],[2508.39,"But what he's getting at is the fact that the things that we think, again, remember the last shall be first and the first shall be last."],[2517.43,"The things we tend to think of and value in this life, that we tend to think of as helpful, can spiritually become a great obstacle to us in terms of the kingdom of heaven."],[2533.43,"And some of the things which we think of as negative in this life, like poverty, can actually be blessings in helping to draw us closer to God."],[2553.03,"This isn't a new insight."],[2555.19,"Remember, this goes all the way back."],[2557.99,"All the way back into the Old Testament, all the way back into the Torah."],[2561.11,"Remember what God said in Deuteronomy was going to happen after he brought them into the land."],[2565.11,"He said, I'm about to bring you in the land."],[2567.59,"And once I've given you the land, and you've built your vineyards and you've built your farms and you're settled there, you're going to get rich and you're going to get fat and you're going to forget about me."],[2582.23,"You're going to forget you were ever slaves in Egypt."],[2584.55,"You're going to forget what I've done for you."],[2586.87,"You're going to forget that I gave you this land."],[2590.47,"Right. You're going to forget me, and then it's all going to fall apart."],[2597.67,"It's all going to fall apart."],[2599.91,"Not because God was going to get angry at them for forgetting him, but because when you forget me, you're going to forget my law."],[2608.47,"You're going to start lying, you're gonna start cheating, you're gonna start stealing, you're gonna start worshiping other gods, participating in these pagan rituals."],[2619.79,"You're gonna start marrying multiple wives, you're gonna start doing all these things, your families are gonna fall apart, your social structure is gonna fall apart."],[2629.95,"The kings who rule over you are gonna become tyrants because they're gonna forget my law."],[2634.19,"This whole thing's gonna go south."],[2639.71,"None of us wants to get sick."],[2645.07,"When I'm sick, I'll be honest, I tend to pray more than when I'm healthy."],[2654.75,"When I'm having money problems, I tend to pray more than when I'm flush."],[2666.99,"When I'm sick than when I'm healthy."],[2684.03,"And the rest of the time, when there's not a problem, I forget."],[2687.31,"Just like Israel forgot."],[2690.43,"And so in this way, these things that are called be called later in the epistles trials of various kinds, temptations, hardships."],[2701.23,"These things can be blessings to us because they remind us of God."],[2705.47,"They remind us of who God is."],[2706.83,"They remind us to be thankful for things that we take for granted."],[2710.99,"A few years ago, when all of a sudden we couldn't drink the water around here or take showers."],[2720.79,"All of a sudden I realize what a blessing it is to have hot and cold running water."],[2727.75,"Yeah. Which I had taken for granted pretty much my whole life."],[2735.19,"And so these things can actually be blessings."],[2739.19,"And the flip side of that is those things we think are blessings."],[2745.51,"We come into a bunch of money."],[2747.43,"When things are going well, when we get the promotion."],[2751.35,"All these things that we think of as good things, if they cause us to forget God, they cause us to forget his law, they cause us to sort of wander off and depend on our own understanding and our own wherewithal."],[2764.31,"Can actually be curses in terms of the big picture, in terms of the kingdom of God, in terms of eternal life."],[2770.31,"That's what St."],[2771.11,"Luke is getting at."],[2776.23,"Now, a lot of people who preach on this and teach on this, this is one of those things that people like to relatize."],[2785.83,"Let's go sell everything you have and give it to the poor thing."],[2788.47,"That was just for this one guy."],[2789.59,"Jesus was just making a point."],[2791.11,"I don't have to do that."],[2793.35,"Right. It's okay for me to be rich."],[2797.35,"You're just making a point."],[2801.35,"This has to do fundamentally with our approach to the scriptures."],[2806.39,"When we read the scriptures and we see a commandment like this that we can't keep, the correct way to respond to that is to say, there's a commandment here that I can't keep because I'm weak."],[2822.51,"I need to do better about this."],[2824.75,"I need to do better about spending less money, you know, stuffing my gut, and more money giving to the poor and helping people."],[2833.71,"I need to work on not collecting so much stuff."],[2839.71,"And putting the money to better use for the kingdom of God."],[2844.19,"But what it's important that we don't do is try and relativize it or excuse ourselves."],[2851.23,"Because where do we end up if we do that?"],[2855.23,"We end up with the Pharisee."],[2858.75,"We end up with this young ruler."],[2860.43,"Oh, I've done everything I needed to do."],[2862.83,"I've kept the whole law."],[2864.59,"Because everything I can't keep, I've explained away somehow."],[2869.31,"Right? We sort of lower the bar so that we could step over it."],[2875.47,"Rather than just admitting the bar's too high for me."],[2881.31,"And I need to work on it."],[2887.15,"We're about to see that the people who heard it originally understood that."],[2892.67,"Right? Because the people who hear it, their response is not, man, that guy's stupid."],[2897.47,"Trading eternal life for stuff."],[2900.19,"Right? Or, yeah, those no good rich people, stick it to them, Jesus."],[2905.47,"Occupy Judea. Right?"],[2909.07,"That's not where they go."],[2911.71,"Their response is those who heard it said, who then can be saved?"],[2916.99,"Right. They saw this interaction."],[2922.67,"Where this guy says, Yeah, I can't, I can't do it."],[2924.11,"I can't sell everything I have and give it to the poor."],[2928.47,"And Jesus says, Well, it's real hard for somebody rich like you to get saved."],[2931.91,"They're like, Well, uh, we're all in trouble."],[2935.91,"Because I'm not ready to do that either."],[2939.35,"Right. But he said, the things which are impossible with men are possible with God."],[2948.47,"Which says two things."],[2949.67,"Number one, you're right."],[2952.31,"You can't do it."],[2953.75,"The bar is too high for you to jump it."],[2957.83,"Right. But don't fall into despair."],[2963.91,"Right? Because though it's impossible for you, it is possible for God to do it."],[2970.95,"This is the beginning."],[2972.39,"What Jesus is saying here is the beginning of the fulfillment of what we saw in Jeremiah chapter 31."],[2977.91,"When Jeremiah prophesied about the new covenant."],[3000.55,"Jesus saying, Yeah, there's the bar."],[3004.15,"You try and jump that bar, you're gonna fall on your face or hit the bar, or it's not gonna go well."],[3014.79,"No. Not and have it count."],[3019.35,"Right. So. Right now, no limbo under this bar."],[3025.99,"But right, but God can accomplish this."],[3029.03,"You can't earn eternal life."],[3033.71,"So it's a good thing for you that God wants to give it to you."],[3038.19,"That God wants to share it with."],[3042.99,"But that doesn't make the bar disappear."],[3046.43,"Or lower the bar one centimeter."],[3051.47,"Just means we give thanks to God for our salvation."],[3054.75,"Not take credit for it ourselves, like the Pharisee."],[3063.87,"Then Peter said, Here comes St."],[3066.75,"Peter again. Right?"],[3069.47,"He's always ready to pipe up and throw his two cents in."],[3072.51,"Right? So these people were all worried."],[3074.67,"They're all like, oh man, what are we going to do?"],[3076.35,"We gotta do that."],[3076.99,"We're in trouble."],[3078.59,"St. Peter says, Peter said, See, we have left all and followed you."],[3084.03,"Like, see, Jesus, we did it."],[3086.91,"Yay! Go us."],[3088.83,"Right. Alright. You know?"],[3094.43,"So he said to them, Assuredly I say to you, there is no one who has left house or parents or brothers or wife or children for the sake of the kingdom of God, who shall not receive many times more in this present time and in the age to come eternal life."],[3110.27,"Now, what he's saying there is not, you left one wife, so I'm gonna give you three."],[3114.51,"That's not what he's saying."],[3118.43,"But the point he's making, what he's making, right, is again, the offer he made to that returning ruler was serious."],[3130.83,"It's serious. He's telling St."],[3133.15,"Peter, Yes, you are on the path that leads to salvation."],[3139.83,"He's not saying you earned it yourself."],[3141.51,"He's not saying congratulations."],[3144.23,"But he's saying, Yeah."],[3147.83,"Yeah. He's reiterating what he said before."],[3151.27,"This is the path that leads to salvation."],[3153.35,"Leaving everything in this world behind."],[3158.39,"And follow Christ."],[3161.99,"That's it. That's the path that leads to eternal life."],[3168.79,"Then he took the twelve aside and said to them, this is an important qualifier on what he just said."],[3174.31,"Notice he doesn't say this to everybody."],[3176.07,"There are these people standing by who heard the interchange of the room."],[3179.11,"Now he just takes his disciples."],[3182.87,"Notice again it says the twelve."],[3185.03,"It's going to be important later."],[3186.39,"Judas is there too."],[3188.63,"And you gotta remember, when he sends the twelve out to do miracles, Judas is out there doing miracles too."],[3194.71,"When his disciples are baptizing, Judas is out there baptizing people too."],[3198.47,"I know that would be lame if you were one of those people who got baptized by Judas."],[3203.75,"Then we have to get into the theology of the sacraments, but that's a whole other, a whole other rabbit trail."],[3209.59,"Right? When Jesus is teaching his disciples, Judas is there hearing it all too."],[3216.47,"Jesus doesn't exclude Judas."],[3218.79,"Judas is going to end up excluding himself."],[3225.83,"So, all 12 of them, he calls them off to the side."],[3228.39,"He says, Behold, we are going up to Jerusalem, and all things that are written by the prophets concerning the Son of Man will be accomplished."],[3236.31,"For he will be delivered to the Gentiles and will be mocked and insulted and spit upon."],[3241.07,"They will scourge him and kill him, and the third day he will rise again."],[3247.63,"The reason I say this is an important qualifier to what he just said to Peter is he just said to Peter, Yes, you are on the road that leads to eternal life."],[3257.55,"By the way, this is where that road leads through."],[3262.59,"Right? You're following me."],[3264.43,"This is where I'm going."],[3269.23,"So before you think, alright, I'm in."],[3273.87,"Right? This is what you're in for."],[3277.63,"This is what you're in for."],[3281.87,"It's also important to remember."],[3284.59,"This is one of several, your Orthodox Study Bible there."],[3287.23,"If you're looking at it, you notice it says this is the third time Jesus is explicitly said this."],[3292.59,"Remember, part of what's going on here is this isn't something bad that happens to Jesus."],[3298.59,"Right? Jesus walks into Jerusalem with the best intentions."],[3302.83,"Right? Preaching and hoping everyone will come and follow him, and oh man, it all goes wrong."],[3309.55,"Jesus has known full well this whole time what's going to happen when he gets to Jerusalem."],[3313.47,"He's not just being a pessimist."],[3315.87,"Man, when we get to Jerusalem, they're probably gonna kill me."],[3318.83,"Right? He's not just being Eeyore."],[3322.83,"Okay. This is he knows what's happening, and he's going there deliberately to do this."],[3329.39,"That's part of what St."],[3330.43,"Luke is communicating to us."],[3333.63,"He knows he's going there in order for this to happen."],[3337.39,"That's why he points out, these are all the things that the prophets said were going to happen."],[3342.51,"Right? Those prophets who told you there was going to be a Messiah."],[3347.27,"If you read them carefully, you know this is what's going to happen to them."],[3352.15,"This is what makes me the Messiah."],[3355.11,"This is the mission of the Messiah, and I'm going there to fulfill it."],[3358.55,"Not to ride in and overthrow the Romans."],[3362.23,"But this. And as we should expect from the disciples now, but they understood none of these things."],[3371.99,"The saying was hidden from them."],[3373.99,"And they did not know the things which were spoken."],[3378.07,"So, disciples, even though this is the third time Jesus has run through it, still clueless."],[3383.59,"Quit being down in the dumps, Jesus, it's gonna go great."],[3386.23,"Don't worry about it."],[3390.31,"They don't understand what he's saying."],[3394.31,"Now we have a little bit of a break in the text."],[3396.87,"We've got a then it happened."],[3399.27,"Which we've talked about before."],[3401.51,"Okay. So what did Jesus just say?"],[3404.23,"We're going up to Jerusalem."],[3406.07,"Now we're entering into sort of the end game here of St."],[3410.47,"Luke's gospel. They're in Judea."],[3413.11,"Now they're headed for Jerusalem."]],"o":[{"t":0.3,"lv":2,"h":"Recap: where we are in Luke","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Pick up <b>Luke 18:15</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Intro to Luke = very first Bible study, on the website</li><li class=\"d0\">Broad strokes of Luke</li><li class=\"d1\">prologue: births of <b>John the Forerunner</b> and Christ</li><li class=\"d1\">ministry begins in <b>Galilee</b> → journey through <b>Samaria</b> → <b>Judea</b></li><li class=\"d1\">now teaching in Judea on the way to <b>Jerusalem</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Getting close - \"probably before we finish tonight, at least on the <b>outskirts</b> of the city\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Since Judea: a series of sections recounting his <b>teaching</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>dinner party</b> at the Pharisees' house</li><li class=\"d1\">other exchanges with <b>Pharisees</b>, disciples, people following</li><li class=\"d0\">In the midst of one of those sections now</li></ul>"},{"t":121.06,"lv":2,"h":"Aside: the \"original text\" presupposition","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Note because of questions - \"I'll call it a <b>problem</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Books, <b>TV documentaries</b>, <b>YouTube</b> (\"no quality control\") on the Bible</li><li class=\"d0\">Presupposition: the <b>earliest, oldest</b> form of the text = the <b>best / real</b> form</li><li class=\"d1\">sometimes goes further: get <b>behind the text</b> to \"what really happened\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Same root as <b>harmonizing the gospels</b> - smushing four into one story</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>John</b>: temple cleansing near the <b>beginning</b>; other three: at the <b>end</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>St. John Chrysostom</b>: cleansed it <b>twice</b> - \"long pedigree\"</li><li class=\"d1\">but none of the four says twice → \"your own version that corresponds to <b>none of the four</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>seven last words</b> from the cross - none says seven; tally the four → \"will destroy a lot of nice sermons and Easter pageants\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Rougher version: <b>History / National Geographic</b> - \"none of this really happened, here's the <b>historical Jesus</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">same thing - another version beyond the four</li><li class=\"d0\">Chopping the text: \"not in the oldest manuscripts\"</li><li class=\"d1\">boy and the demon: \"this kind comes out only by prayer\" - <b>\"and fasting\"</b> not in earliest - \"as much as I'd like to leave that out, as you can tell from looking at me\"</li><li class=\"d1\">assumption: not \"original\" → \"we can ignore it\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>sweating blood</b> in Luke (coming up) - not in the oldest manuscripts</li></ul>"},{"t":454.86,"lv":3,"h":"Problem 1: no access; Problem 2: what is \"the original\"?","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>1.</b> No access to \"what really happened\" other than the <b>four gospels</b></li><li class=\"d1\">anything else = <b>conjecture</b>, \"making it up, guessing\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>2.</b> \"The Bible is the Bible\" - more you study, <b>messier</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"it's the original that has authority\" → test with <b>2 Corinthians</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Paul <b>dictates</b>; <b>scribe</b> writes - secretary also <b>corrects grammar</b>?</li><li class=\"d1\">dictator reads over, <b>corrects</b>, signs (\"see, I'm writing this with my own hand\")</li><li class=\"d1\">original = what came out of his mouth? scribe's text? the corrected version?</li><li class=\"d0\">2 Corinthians = parts of <b>two letters</b> put together (Paul wrote <b>four</b> to Corinth)</li><li class=\"d1\">original = two letters entire, or just the parts?</li><li class=\"d0\">~<b>100 AD</b>: Christians collected <b>all Paul's letters and Hebrews</b>, edited together</li><li class=\"d1\">why \"St. Paul's Epistle to the Hebrews\" - fathers said \"doesn't look like same guy\", but in the collection</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>every</b> extant copy of 2 Corinthians is from <b>that collection</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"pursue the original… <b>doesn't work</b>\"</li></ul>"},{"t":708.66,"lv":2,"h":"The version with authority is the one the church has used","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Another tautology: the version with authority <b>in the church</b> = the version with authority in the church</li><li class=\"d0\">Close to <b>6,000 manuscripts</b> of NT - handwritten, <b>2nd to 15th c.</b></li><li class=\"d1\">none identical - spelling mistakes, left-out word, <b>skipped a line</b> late at night, skipped a page</li><li class=\"d1\">but with <b>5,999 others</b> you can tell → \"not like we don't know what it says\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Many branches of the stream, but <b>one stream</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>read, prayed, quoted</b> by the church for <b>2,000 years</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Authority ≠ a hypothetical <b>original</b> or hypothetical <b>event</b> → it is the version that <b>has had authority</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Hence \"<b>thine is the kingdom, power and glory</b>\" at end of Lord's Prayer: <b>added by the church</b> later - not a problem for us</li><li class=\"d0\">Orthodox don't believe God inspired <b>Paul one day in 45 AD</b> to write <b>Galatians</b>, then threw it into the world</li><li class=\"d1\">\"do the best we can\" to work out what the Spirit said? No</li><li class=\"d1\">same <b>Holy Spirit</b> inspired Paul, lives in the church, was with the <b>copyists, readers, preachers, fathers</b></li><li class=\"d1\">scriptures we have now = what God has given us <b>now</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Archaeology: \"interesting to <b>nerds like me</b>\" - how text developed, fathers quoting a verse differently</li><li class=\"d1\">not germane to which version has authority for <b>how we live</b> and know Christ</li></ul>"},{"t":963.46,"lv":3,"h":"Why this matters - Protestant inerrancy debates","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Questions from people; need to be able to give somebody an answer</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Protestant friends</b> spend huge time arguing: <b>inerrancy</b>, \"inerrant in the originals\" - \"we don't have the originals\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>fundamentalist vs liberal</b> debate</li><li class=\"d1\">bogged down → <b>don't hear what Scripture says</b></li><li class=\"d1\">arguing whether the <b>Exodus</b> happened exactly so, what year, which Pharaoh → miss the point</li><li class=\"d0\">Text teaches: <b>how God deals with his people</b>; more specifically, <b>Christ</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Luke ahead: Christ dies and rises at <b>Passover</b> - \"not a coincidence\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"miss the forest for the trees\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Not an argument we need to have</li><li class=\"d1\">Scriptures given through the <b>Holy Spirit</b>, to lead us to Christ - study them <b>as we have them</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1093.74,"lv":2,"h":"Christ is still with us: Protestant, Catholic, Orthodox","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Footnote: through the <b>Holy Spirit</b>, Christ is <b>still with us</b></li><li class=\"d1\">liturgy: \"Christ is in our midst\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Protestant</b>: ascended and <b>left us a book</b> - the Bible is how we know Christ, worship, everything</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Roman Catholic</b>: ascended and sent a <b>vicar</b> - Peter in charge, passed on</li><li class=\"d1\">Pope / <b>magisterium</b> tells you what's true, what the Bible is, what it means, what tradition is</li><li class=\"d0\">Neither is what Scripture says: Christ ascended and <b>left the Holy Spirit</b> (just celebrated the <b>Ascension</b>)</li><li class=\"d1\">Spirit continues to reveal Christ through <b>Scriptures and the church</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Tradition</b> = <b>life of the Holy Spirit in the church</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not \"something bishops whisper in back rooms\"</li><li class=\"d1\">the Spirit in every generation since the beginning</li><li class=\"d0\">So we trust the Scriptures: not <b>historical accidents</b> but the <b>working of the Holy Spirit</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1255.1,"lv":2,"h":"Q&amp;A: Explaining the Holy Spirit to Protestants","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Q: how to explain with them, given their mindset?</li><li class=\"d0\">Issue is <b>Western theology</b>, not just Protestantism</li><li class=\"d1\">innately <b>binitarian</b> (two, not three) - because of the <b>Filioque</b>: Spirit proceeds from Father <b>and Son</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Arians</b>: Son <b>begotten</b>, Spirit <b>proceeds</b> → only the Father is really God</li><li class=\"d1\">\"bad argument\" - <b>circular</b>: Father is Father because <b>unbegotten, doesn't proceed</b></li><li class=\"d1\">West's response: <b>Filioque</b> - Father and Son both <b>sources of divinity</b></li><li class=\"d1\">problem: <b>who proceeds from the Holy Spirit?</b> - by their definition is the Spirit God?</li><li class=\"d0\">Result: Spirit <b>demoted</b>, subordinate status by the construct (they'd deny it)</li><li class=\"d1\">to be God you must be a <b>source of Godhead</b>; Spirit isn't</li><li class=\"d0\">So in Protestant and much <b>Roman Catholic</b> theology the Spirit is <b>depersonalized</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"like the <b>Force</b> in Star Wars\" - a feeling, an energy</li><li class=\"d1\">personhood and place in the Trinity vanish</li><li class=\"d0\">Shows up either as <b>Pentecostalism</b> (only the Spirit) or most Protestant churches (<b>barely mention</b> him; almost all Christ)</li></ul>"},{"t":1486.54,"lv":3,"h":"How to respond - start with the Trinity","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Start a step back: the <b>Holy Trinity</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>three persons</b>, equally God; <b>one God</b>; unity found in the <b>Father</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"gets very deep… I went into the weeds\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Take them in Scripture to <b>John 16-19</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Christ on <b>sending the Spirit</b>, what the Spirit will do, how he works in the church</li><li class=\"d1\">how he speaks of the Spirit relating to <b>him</b> and to the <b>Father</b></li><li class=\"d1\">best place to start them thinking about the Trinity differently</li></ul>"},{"t":1578.74,"lv":2,"h":"Luke 18:15-16 - Infants brought to Jesus","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"They also brought <b>infants</b> that he might touch them\"; disciples <b>rebuked</b> them</li><li class=\"d0\">Ancient view of children vs today</li><li class=\"d1\">we: babies cute, <b>pad the whole world</b>, scrutinize TV</li><li class=\"d1\">ancient world: \"not that way\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Roman family: <b>abortion</b>, and <b>exposure of infants</b></li><li class=\"d1\">baby brought to the <i>pater familias</i> = father of the family</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>extended family</b>: mom, dad, kids, grandkids, uncle, aunt, cousin</li><li class=\"d1\">head = patriarch, grandpa / great-grandpa</li><li class=\"d1\">he <b>inspects</b>, thinks economically, who the father was → accept or not</li><li class=\"d1\">not accepted → <b>left in the woods to die</b></li><li class=\"d0\">1st-c. letters: husband to wife who just had baby: \"<b>if a boy, keep it; if a girl, take care of it</b>\" = abandon it</li><li class=\"d1\">\"common and accepted\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Early Christians <b>found and adopted</b> these babies - completely opposed</li></ul>"},{"t":1748.82,"lv":3,"h":"Children as a nuisance - why the disciples rebuked them","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Kids not seen as a <b>blessing from God</b> - up to you whether to raise; if not, \"get rid of it\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"kind of a <b>nuisance</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Jews</b> by and large did not</li><li class=\"d1\">maybe Hellenized Jews elsewhere in the empire</li><li class=\"d1\">in <b>Judea</b> frowned upon</li><li class=\"d0\">Kids in the streets: \"one step up from <b>stray dogs</b>\", running around begging</li><li class=\"d0\">Disciples not \"grumpy old men\" - \"young punks, get off my lawn\"</li><li class=\"d1\">reflecting <b>societal attitude</b></li><li class=\"d1\">shoo them off like a <b>stray dog or cat</b> begging</li></ul>"},{"t":1837.71,"lv":3,"h":"Luke 18:16-17 - \"Of such is the kingdom of God\"","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Jesus <b>called the disciples</b> (the \"them\") to him</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Let the little children come to me, <b>do not forbid them</b>, for such is the kingdom of God\"</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Whoever does not receive the kingdom as a little child will <b>by no means enter it</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Don't read through <b>modern view</b>: innocent, kind, trusting, loving - not the view then</li><li class=\"d0\">Illustration of the <b>last first, first last</b> from recent passages</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Pharisee and publican</b> - one thought himself great, the other realized he wasn't much, asked for <b>mercy</b></li><li class=\"d1\">cast-off kids, <b>dependents</b> = like the publican</li><li class=\"d0\">Set yourself in the <b>lowest place</b> to enter the kingdom</li><li class=\"d1\">= <b>humility</b> - not \"sweet, innocent, cute\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Next: another example, <b>in the other direction</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1984.43,"lv":2,"h":"Luke 18:18-19 - The ruler: \"Good teacher\"","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"A certain <b>ruler</b>: <b>Good teacher</b>, what shall I do to <b>inherit eternal life</b>?\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Greek <i>archon</i> - better \"<b>leader</b>\", leading citizen</li><li class=\"d1\">prominent in <b>Judea</b> - not a Roman citizen</li><li class=\"d1\">not the <b>peasants from Galilee</b> - \"one of the important people\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Jesus: \"<b>Why do you call me good? No one is good but one, that is God</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">is he saying he's not good? → he's saying <b>he is God</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"Good teacher\" = a bit of kissing up, respectful - but is Jesus just a good rabbi?</li><li class=\"d1\">\"collecting <b>spiritual advice</b>\" - opinions from other rabbis, now this one</li><li class=\"d1\">no: Jesus is <b>questioning the man's approach</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Jesus answers <b>authoritatively</b></li><li class=\"d1\">never \"think about this, decide if it's useful, maybe not\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"Jesus doesn't give advice. He gives <b>authoritative instruction</b>\"</li></ul>"},{"t":2153.91,"lv":3,"h":"18:20-21 - \"You know the commandments\"","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Quotes the Ten Commandments: <b>adultery, murder, steal, false witness, honor father and mother</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Why \"you know\"? Still questioning his approach</li><li class=\"d1\">prominent person, been to <b>synagogue</b>, heard the law</li><li class=\"d1\">Deuteronomy: \"he who does these things will <b>live by them</b>\" - keep the commandments</li><li class=\"d1\">\"Why are you asking me? You should already know\"</li><li class=\"d0\">\"<b>All these I have kept from my youth</b>\" - sounds like the <b>Pharisee</b> (\"I fast, I tithe… I'm righteous\")</li><li class=\"d1\">comes \"as an equal\": \"What's your opinion?\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"since I was a child\" - \"he was a teenager at some point, so <b>we know that's a lie</b>\"</li></ul>"},{"t":2287.95,"lv":3,"h":"18:22-23 - \"Sell all that you have\"","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"When Jesus heard…\" - now he knows who this person is</li><li class=\"d0\">\"You still lack <b>one thing</b>\" - for sake of argument, you've kept all</li><li class=\"d1\">\"<b>Sell all you have, distribute to the poor</b>, treasure in heaven, <b>come follow me</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">wealthy prominent citizen → become one of my <b>disciples</b> → inherit eternal life</li><li class=\"d0\">Sarcastic? <b>No</b> - \"an honest answer\": if he does this, he will inherit eternal life</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Very sorrowful, for he was <b>very rich</b>\" - \"gotta keep your stuff\"</li></ul>"},{"t":2384.15,"lv":2,"h":"Luke 18:24-25 - Camel and the eye of a needle","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Jesus saw his response - visibly distraught (\"<b>sad face emoji</b>\") because he wouldn't do it</li><li class=\"d0\">\"How hard…\" - \"easier for a <b>camel</b> through the <b>eye of a needle</b> than a rich man into the kingdom\"</li><li class=\"d1\">usually: actual needle and thread</li><li class=\"d1\">debate: a small <b>gate</b> of the city - either way \"very difficult\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Medici family</b> - insanely wealthy 16th-17th c. - family chapel on their estates (still in Italy)</li><li class=\"d1\">wanted to communicate that they were <b>going to make it</b> anyway</li><li class=\"d0\">Recurring theme in Luke</li><li class=\"d1\">Matthew 5 \"blessed are the <b>poor in spirit</b>\" → Luke: \"blessed are the <b>poor</b>. Period.\"</li><li class=\"d1\">Luke speaks more <b>literally</b> about wealth and poverty</li><li class=\"d0\">Not \"wealthy bad, poor good\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>last first, first last</b>: what we value and think helpful can become a <b>great obstacle</b> to the kingdom</li><li class=\"d1\">what we think negative - <b>poverty</b> - can be a <b>blessing</b>, draws us to God</li></ul>"},{"t":2553.03,"lv":3,"h":"Deuteronomy: rich, fat, forget me - and trials as blessings","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Old insight - back to the <b>Torah</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Deuteronomy</b>: once in the land - vineyards, farms, settled → \"<b>rich, fat, forget me</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">forget you were slaves in Egypt, what I did, that I gave the land</li><li class=\"d1\">not because God gets angry - you forget <b>my law</b></li><li class=\"d1\">start lying, cheating, stealing, <b>other gods</b>, pagan rituals, <b>multiple wives</b></li><li class=\"d1\">families and social structure fall apart; kings become <b>tyrants</b>; \"whole thing goes south\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Nobody wants to get sick - \"when I'm sick I <b>pray more</b> than when healthy\"; money problems → pray more than when flush</li><li class=\"d1\">rest of the time: \"I forget. Just like <b>Israel</b> forgot\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Trials, temptations, hardships</b> (epistles) = blessings: remind us of God, to be <b>thankful</b> for what we take for granted</li><li class=\"d1\">a few years ago, couldn't drink the water or shower → \"what a blessing <b>hot and cold running water</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Flip side: money, promotion, things going well → if we <b>forget God and his law</b>, depend on <b>our own understanding</b> → <b>curses</b> in the big picture of eternal life</li></ul>"},{"t":2776.23,"lv":2,"h":"Don't relativize the commandment","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Common move: \"sell everything\" was <b>just for this one guy</b>; \"it's okay for me to be rich\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Fundamentally about <b>approach to Scripture</b></li><li class=\"d1\">commandment I can't keep → say \"I can't because <b>I'm weak</b>, I need to do better\"</li><li class=\"d1\">spend less on \"stuffing my gut\", more on the <b>poor</b>; not collect so much stuff; money for the kingdom</li><li class=\"d0\">Don't <b>relativize or excuse ourselves</b></li><li class=\"d1\">→ end up the <b>Pharisee</b>, the <b>young ruler</b>: \"I've kept the whole law\" because everything else I've <b>explained away</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"lower the bar so we can step over it\" instead of admitting \"the bar's too high for me\"</li></ul>"},{"t":2887.15,"lv":2,"h":"Luke 18:26-27 - \"Who then can be saved?\"","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Original hearers understood: not \"that guy's stupid, trading eternal life for stuff\"</li><li class=\"d1\">not \"<b>stick it to them, Jesus - Occupy Judea</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Response: \"<b>Who then can be saved?</b>\" - \"we're all in trouble, I'm not ready to do that either\"</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Things impossible with men are possible with God\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>1.</b> you're right - you can't; bar too high to jump</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>2.</b> don't fall into <b>despair</b> - possible for <b>God</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Beginning of fulfillment of <b>Jeremiah 31</b> - the <b>new covenant</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Bar picture: try to jump → fall on your face or hit it; \"no limbo under this bar\"</li><li class=\"d1\">God can accomplish it - <b>you can't earn eternal life</b></li><li class=\"d1\">good thing God <b>wants to give it</b>, share it</li><li class=\"d1\">doesn't <b>lower the bar one centimeter</b></li><li class=\"d1\">→ <b>give thanks</b> for salvation; don't take credit like the <b>Pharisee</b></li></ul>"},{"t":3063.87,"lv":2,"h":"Luke 18:28-30 - Peter: \"We have left all\"","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"Here comes <b>St. Peter</b> again\" - \"always ready to pipe up and throw in his two cents\"</li><li class=\"d1\">the crowd worried: \"what are we going to do?\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Peter: \"<b>See, we have left all and followed you</b>\" - \"Yay, go us\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Jesus: no one who left <b>house, parents, brothers, wife, children</b> for the kingdom who won't receive <b>many times more</b> now and <b>eternal life</b> in the age to come</li><li class=\"d1\">not \"you left one wife, I'll give you three\"</li><li class=\"d0\">The offer to the ruler was <b>serious</b></li><li class=\"d1\">to Peter: yes, you're on the <b>path that leads to salvation</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not \"you earned it\"; not \"congratulations\"</li><li class=\"d1\">path = <b>leave everything behind and follow Christ</b></li></ul>"},{"t":3168.79,"lv":2,"h":"Luke 18:31 - He takes the twelve aside","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"Took the <b>twelve</b> aside\" - an important qualifier on what he just said</li><li class=\"d1\">not to everybody - the bystanders heard the exchange</li><li class=\"d0\">\"The twelve\" - <b>Judas is there too</b></li><li class=\"d1\">sent out to do <b>miracles</b> - Judas did miracles</li><li class=\"d1\">disciples baptizing - Judas baptized (lame if you were baptized by him - \"theology of the sacraments, a whole other rabbit trail\")</li><li class=\"d1\">Judas hears all the teaching</li><li class=\"d1\">\"Jesus doesn't exclude Judas. Judas is going to end up <b>excluding himself</b>\"</li></ul>"},{"t":3225.83,"lv":3,"h":"18:31-33 - Third prediction of the Passion","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"<b>Behold, we are going up to Jerusalem</b>\"; all the prophets wrote about the Son of Man will be <b>accomplished</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>delivered to the Gentiles</b>, mocked, insulted, <b>spit upon</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>scourge</b> him, <b>kill</b> him, <b>third day he will rise</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Qualifier to what he said to Peter</li><li class=\"d1\">yes, you're on the road to eternal life; \"by the way, this is where that road <b>leads through</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"before you think, alright, I'm in - <b>this is what you're in for</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Third explicit time</b> (Orthodox Study Bible note)</li><li class=\"d0\">Not something bad that happens to Jesus</li><li class=\"d1\">not \"walks in with best intentions, hoping everyone follows, oh man, it all goes wrong\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"known full well\" - not being <b>Eeyore</b></li><li class=\"d1\">goes there <b>deliberately</b> - what Luke communicates</li><li class=\"d0\">\"All things written by the <b>prophets</b>\" - those who said there'd be a Messiah</li><li class=\"d1\">read carefully → this is what happens to him</li><li class=\"d1\">\"this is what makes me the <b>Messiah</b>\" - mission he's going to fulfill</li><li class=\"d1\">not to ride in and <b>overthrow the Romans</b></li></ul>"},{"t":3362.23,"lv":3,"h":"Luke 18:34 - Disciples understood nothing","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"Understood none of these things. The saying was <b>hidden</b> from them\"</li><li class=\"d1\">they did not know what was said</li><li class=\"d0\">Third time through, still <b>clueless</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"quit being down in the dumps, Jesus, it's gonna go great\"</li><li class=\"d0\">A <b>break in the text</b> - \"then it happened\" (<b>conjunction</b>)</li><li class=\"d1\">after \"we're going up to Jerusalem\" → entering the <b>end game</b> of Luke</li><li class=\"d1\">\"in Judea, now headed for Jerusalem\" - recording ends here</li></ul>"}]});
